' Shared shape for a single Receiver instance's core (the process plus its
' RabbitMQ offline-fallback queue and drain arrows) -- identical for every
' Receiver instance regardless of what it's ingesting (local SDR hardware
' vs. a remote MLAT provider). Defined once here and instantiated with
' distinct aliases per diagram so receiver.puml and
' receiver-mlat-topology.puml don't hand-duplicate this shape.
!procedure $receiverCore($comp_alias, $fallback_alias)
component "Receiver\n--\nTags: raw, icao_hex, received_at, source\nRoutes: adsb-{icao_hex_int % PROCESSOR_COUNT}" as $comp_alias
database "queue.db\n(SQLite WAL)" as $fallback_alias
$comp_alias -right-> $fallback_alias : RabbitMQ offline
$fallback_alias .left.> $comp_alias : Drains on RabbitMQ reconnect\nor every telemetry tick
!endprocedure
